// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : texts/Working 	Sheet : Vanguard_Ep7Contact 
//
// Script      : Xlstocontactdef.bat 
// Version     : 35 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Infernia 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P183708272" "Infernia"
// ProfessionString :
// DescriptionString :
"P454968318" "Infernia and her twin sister Glacia spent years battling each other before the Rikti attacked. United for the first time, they fought side-by-side and together volunteered to join the Omega team. Like all members of the Omega team, their fate had been a mystery until they were rescued by Lady Grey and a team of super-powered individuals.<br><br>Infernia has been working with Vanguard to fortify their efforts against inter-dimensional threats."
// LocationString :
"P980288551" "Rikti War Zone"
// InteractionRequiresText :
"P3192533869" "<color orange>You need to purchase the seventh episode of the first signature story arc, <i>Who Will Die</i>, in order to play Infernia's story arc.</color>"
// TaskForceInvite :
"P3066760211" "{HeroName}. We don't have a lot of time to talk. I'm sure you're fully aware of the situation we're all in. Darrin Wade is attempting, as we speak, to summon Rularuu into this world. He has Statesman and Sister Psyche's powers at his disposal and is almost impossible to beat.<br><br>Wade's whole plan has left the Freedom Phalanx and Vindicators a wreck, so they're both out of the picture. Vanguard is dealing with reports of Rularuu monsters appearing all over the world, <i>except</i> for Paragon and the Isles. Seems like Wade is doing his best to keep everyone as spread out as possible.<br><br>That leaves <i>you</i> and a select few who may have the capabilities of actually stopping Darrin Wade before his plans come to fruition. As always, Vanguard is ready to do whatever it takes to face off against inter-dimensional threats. I have a few ideas of how we can handle this. Are you ready to take the fight to Darrin Wade and end this once and for all?<br><br><color orange>This arc contains elite bosses, which may be difficult to defeat by yourself.</color>"
// PlayerLevelTooLow :
"P655500595" "This is cosmic-level stuff, {HeroName}, we'll talk again when your clearance is at least at 40."
// PlayerLevelTooHigh :
// NeedTeamLeader :
"P1267682306" "I've got important things to discuss with your team leader."
// NeedTeamOnMap :
"P3780197889" "Everyone needs to be gathered here before we can get moving."
// BadTeamLevel :
"P3272897955" "Someone in your team isn't the proper clearance for this."
// TaskForceName :
// TaskForceName :
// TaskForceName :
// TaskForceName :
// HelloString :
"P2054941764" "Let's finish this, once and for all."
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

